			<div class="content" id="post-content-1894845">
									

<p>On the one hand, its a pretty straightforward 'non-organic thing turns out to be organic' body horror piece in some respects, and the reproduction part just seems like borderline sloppy expungement to me. However, there are lots of things I rather like about this, like the idea of an anomalous gardener, the stuff about the gardener moving like an earthworm, and the last line.</p>
<p>Overall, I think its a good article even though its in the same vein as several other similar articles, and although it'd be nice to have some of the expungement cleared up, the rest is good enough for me to overlook it. +1</p>

